  ACS CORP — VULNERABILITY REMEDIATION TIMELINE POLICY
  Document ID: ACS-POL-SI-002 | Version: 2.1
  Effective Date: January 1, 2026
  Organization: ACS Corp | Domain: acs-p01.local
====================================================================

1. PURPOSE
----------
This policy establishes maximum acceptable timeframes for remediating
identified information system flaws per NIST SP 800-53 SI-2 and
CMMC Level 1 requirements.

2. SCOPE
--------
All information systems within the ACS Corp environment, including:
- Domain controllers and servers
- End-user workstations
- Network infrastructure devices
- Cloud-hosted services

3. REMEDIATION TIMELINES
-------------------------
Upon discovery of a vulnerability, remediation must be completed
within the following timeframes based on CVSS severity:

  Severity         CVSS Range    Max Remediation Window
  ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Critical         9.0 - 10.0    7 calendar days
  High             7.0 - 8.9    14 calendar days
  Medium           4.0 - 6.9    30 calendar days
  Low              0.1 - 3.9    90 calendar days
  Informational    0.0           Track only (no SLA)

4. COMPLIANCE MEASUREMENT
--------------------------
- "Discovery Date" = date vulnerability first appears in scan results
- "Remediation Date" = date re-scan confirms vulnerability resolved
- "Exposure Window" = Remediation Date minus Discovery Date
- A finding is COMPLIANT if Exposure Window <= Max Remediation Window
- A finding is NON-COMPLIANT if Exposure Window > Max Remediation Window
  OR if Remediation_Date = OPEN and current age exceeds threshold

5. EXCEPTIONS
-------------
- Risk acceptance requires VP-level approval and documented
  compensating controls
- Maximum risk acceptance duration: 90 days (renewable once)
- No exceptions permitted for Critical findings with active exploits

6. FAILED PATCHES
-----------------
IMPORTANT: An attempted patch that FAILS to install does NOT satisfy
the remediation requirement. The vulnerability remains OPEN until
a successful installation is confirmed via re-scan.

7. REFERENCES
-------------
- NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5: SI-2 (Flaw Remediation)
- CMMC Level 1: SI.L1-3.14.1
- ACS Corp Change Management Policy (ACS-POL-CM-001)

